      "title": "Four superconducting cables join two large quantum processors into one",
      "summary": "Researchers linked two large quantum processors with four superconducting cables so that they can work together as a single, larger machine. This matters because building quantum computers from interconnected modules is seen as a promising route to scaling up, and the links must carry fragile quantum information without destroying it. The approach is still at the research stage, and many more processors would have to be joined reliably before it could support practical, large-scale machines.",
